      "worked_solution": "The measure of $∠POQ$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠POS)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠QOS).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nm∠POQ={150}^{∘}-{85}^{∘}={65}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nLet's add this to our diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133186/assets/90977605b8a67a07ccb6f13bcf37ab92c5b8ec2478210e2999a34f77a86df9f4.png)\n\n  \n\nWe can now find the measure of $∠POR:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠POR & =m∠POQ+m∠QOR \\\\  & ={65}^{∘}+{55}^{∘} \\\\  & ={120}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
